# lucoze-platform bench environment reference (8-app monorepo — 5 GTM bundles)
# ============================================================================
# This file is a CHECKLIST of every env var the merged compose yaml references.
# The actual values live in TWO places, NEVER in git:
#
#   1. Dokploy UI → lucoze-platform (UAT) application → Environment tab
#      → paste each KEY=VALUE pair from below with real values.
#      Dokploy injects them at container start.
#
#   2. ~/gitops/traefik-routes.yaml on the MANAGER VPS
#      → SITES_RULE domains go here (Traefik routing).
#
# Generating the compose yaml to upload to Dokploy (LOCAL machine) — the same
# --no-interpolate pattern as dms (keeps ${VAR} placeholders for the Env tab):
#
#   docker compose \
#     -f compose.yaml \
#     -f overrides/compose.redis.yaml \
#     -f overrides/compose.agent.yaml \
#     config --no-interpolate > /tmp/lucoze-platform.yaml
#
# Paste /tmp/lucoze-platform.yaml into Dokploy → New Application → Docker Compose,
# then fill in the Environment tab from the KEY=VALUE list below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Image -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Built by GitHub Actions (.github/workflows/build-lucoze-platform.yml).
# REUSES the legacy tenant repo: the platform REPLACES legacy lucoze, so the
# soon-idle svasamm/lucoze-tenant repository now holds the monorepo image.
# (The token already has push scope there — no new Docker Hub repo needed.)
CUSTOM_IMAGE=svasamm/lucoze-tenant

# Floating tags (auto-updated by CI on each release — no config change needed):
#   uat-latest   — always points to latest UAT build  (use for UAT bench)
#   latest       — always points to latest production build (use for prod bench)
#
# Pinned tags (immutable, for rollback or audit):
#   uat-v1.0.0-9695448   — exact UAT build  (use to roll back to a known-good)
#   v1.0.0-abc1234       — exact production build
#
# For UAT:
CUSTOM_TAG=uat-latest
# For Production:
# CUSTOM_TAG=latest

# always  = pull on every container start (use for floating tags like uat-latest)
# missing = only pull if image not present locally (use for pinned SHA tags)
PULL_POLICY=always

# --- Database ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Must match DB_PASSWORD in mariadb.env on the SHARED MariaDB container.
DB_HOST=mariadb-database
DB_PORT=3306
DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_SAME_AS_MARIADB_ENV

# --- Bench identity ----------------------------------------------------------
# ROUTER: unique name for this bench (Docker network name + must be unique per
# agent). Distinct from the retired legacy `lucoze` bench.
#
# UAT  → ROUTER=lucoze-platform
# Prod → ROUTER=lucoze-platform-prod   (only when a prod bench is stood up)
ROUTER=lucoze-platform

# --- Agent routing (Option B: Central Traefik on Manager) -------------------
# AGENT_PRIVATE_IP: private-network IP of the Agent VPS this bench runs on.
#   Same Agent as the rest of the estate (10.0.0.2).
AGENT_PRIVATE_IP=10.0.0.2

# BENCH_PORT: frontend port on the private network. Unique per bench per agent.
#
# Current per-agent allocation (see gitops/README.md port table):
#   cafirm            = 8080
#   lucoze-admin      = 8082
#   lucoze (tenant)   = 8083   ← RETIRED (platform replaces legacy)
#   lucoze-website    = 8084
#   dms-uat           = 8085
#   dms (prod)        = 8086
#   lucoze-platform   = 8087   ← THIS bench (UAT)
#
# For UAT:
BENCH_PORT=8087
# For Production (future):
# BENCH_PORT=8088

# --- Domains (for reference — used in Manager Traefik config, not here) ------
# SITES_RULE is NOT used in compose.agent.yaml (no Traefik labels on agent).
# Keep it here as documentation for what to put in ~/gitops/traefik-routes.yaml
# on the Manager. One bench serves all 5 GTM bundles as separate Frappe sites
# (bundle = the app-subset installed on that site).
#
# UAT showcase sites (one per bundle; Pharmacy shares diagnostics host or gets
# its own later):
#   Host(`diagnostics.lucoze.com`) || Host(`polyclinic.lucoze.com`) ||
#   Host(`hospital.lucoze.com`)    || Host(`hospitalent.lucoze.com`)
SITES_RULE=Host(`diagnostics.lucoze.com`) || Host(`polyclinic.lucoze.com`) || Host(`hospital.lucoze.com`) || Host(`hospitalent.lucoze.com`)
